    {
      "id": "bug-007",
      "timestamp": "2026-06-10T17:40:00Z",
      "error_message": "user: 'sometimes it's cleaning up too much' — e.g. spoken 'I sometimes...' written as 'Sometimes...' (leading 'I' dropped); separately saw 'sometimes' become 'times'",
      "file": "crates/talk-core/src/cleanup.rs",
      "root_cause": "TWO distinct causes. (1) Post-processing: strip_leading_fillers used the broad FILLERS set (incl. i/you/so/well/like/know/mean), so a LEADING subject pronoun or discourse opener was dropped as if a disfluency ('I sometimes forget'->'Sometimes forget'). The FILLERS set is meant for the content-word GUARD's both-sides comparison, NOT as a strip list. (2) 'sometimes'->'times' is NOT post-processing — proven: cleanup keeps 'some' in every case (static + dynamic). It is pass-2 Moonshine base occasionally mishearing the word on real voice; the live edge shows pass-1 (zipformer) correct, then the pass-2 revise swaps in the worse word.",
      "fix": "Added LEADING_DISFLUENCIES = [um,uh,er,ah,mm,hmm,uhm,erm,hm] (non-lexical only); strip_leading_fillers now strips ONLY that set (with leading-punct trim), never FILLERS. FILLERS retained unchanged for guard_accepts. Updated 2 tests that encoded the old over-strip (session.rs, format.rs) to the corrected 'So I keep...' output. 'times' case left as a model property, surfaced to user (no blind pass-2 change).",
      "tags": [
        "cleanup",
        "over-cleaning",
        "strip_leading_fillers",
        "transcription",
        "pass-2",
        "moonshine",
        "deterministic_light",
        "restraint"
      ],
      "related_bugs": [],
      "occurrences": 1,
      "last_seen": "2026-06-10T17:40:00Z"
