      "error_message": "user: 'when the cli is starting it doesn't seem to be working in the beginning - ~5s delay'",
      "file": "src/main.rs",
      "root_cause": "Startup hashed 417MB every launch: models_ready() verified the .tar.bz2 ARCHIVES (239MB) AND the extracted weights (178MB). Only the extracted files are loaded; archives are needed only for healing. Plus there was NO loading indicator, so the ~1-2s warm / ~5s cold (cold disk read of 417MB) gap before the alternate-screen UI looked hung, and the mic isn't open yet so the user's first words were lost. Model LOAD itself is only ~0.6s (zipformer 245ms + moonshine 343ms) — not the bottleneck.",
      "fix": "models_ready() now verifies EXTRACTED-first and returns early on the happy path; archives are hashed only when healing is needed (178MB hashed per launch, not 417MB). Added a TTY-gated 'preparing…' line before the gate so a cold start shows feedback. Warm reflect startup 1.86s->1.13s; cold-cache savings larger (178 vs 417MB disk read). Tamper/heal privacy tests unchanged-green.",
